ARM: dts: qcom: apq8064-asus-nexus7-flo: do not offer the SPC idle state

Risk: LOW (gives the same runtime state as today's cpuidle.off=1).

"failed to register cpuidle driver" (x4) is printed by cpuidle_register()
because the kernel is booted with cpuidle.off=1: __cpuidle_register_driver()
returns -ENODEV when cpuidle_disabled() (drivers/cpuidle/driver.c), once per
CPU since cpuidle-qcom-spm registers one driver per CPU. The parameter is
there because entering "qcom,idle-state-spc" hangs this board.

Removing cpu-idle-states makes dt_init_idle_driver() return 0 in
spm_cpuidle_register(), which then returns -ENODEV silently: no cpuidle
driver, CPUs idle in WFI, no error messages, and cpuidle.off=1 can be dropped
from the command line. The SAW regulators used by cpufreq are unaffected.
This is a workaround, not a fix for the SPC hang (see MATRIX.md).
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/qcom-apq8064-asus-nexus7-flo.dts | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-apq8064-asus-nexus7-flo.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-apq8064-asus-nexus7-flo.dts
index e9ea0c9..1ed6d67 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-apq8064-asus-nexus7-flo.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-apq8064-asus-nexus7-flo.dts
@@ -426,6 +426,28 @@
 	};
 };
 
+/*
+ * Entering the SPC idle state hangs this board (boot only completes with
+ * cpuidle.off=1). Until that is understood, do not offer the state: with no
+ * usable DT idle state cpuidle-qcom-spm registers nothing and the CPUs idle
+ * in plain WFI, which is what cpuidle.off=1 gives today.
+ */
+&cpu0 {
+	/delete-property/ cpu-idle-states;
+};
+
+&cpu1 {
+	/delete-property/ cpu-idle-states;
+};
+
+&cpu2 {
+	/delete-property/ cpu-idle-states;
+};
+
+&cpu3 {
+	/delete-property/ cpu-idle-states;
+};
+
 /* The tablet idles around 60 C; start throttling well above that. */
 &cpu_alert0 {
 	temperature = <85000>;
